Smart Farming Robot — Connections Only
Connect the components to your Arduino Uno using these tables. Keep the power OFF while wiring.
1. HC-05 Bluetooth
HC-05	Arduino Uno
VCC	5V*
GND	GND
TXD	D0 (RX)
RXD	D1 (TX), through voltage divider
*Use 5V only if your HC-05 breakout supports it.
Voltage divider for HC-05 RXD: Arduino D1 → 1 kΩ resistor → junction → HC-05 RXD. Connect a 2 kΩ resistor from the junction to GND.
2. L298N motor driver
L298N	Connection
ENA	Arduino D5
IN1	Arduino D7
IN2	Arduino D8
IN3	Arduino D9
IN4	Arduino D10
ENB	Arduino D6
OUT1, OUT2	Left motor
OUT3, OUT4	Right motor
Motor supply +	Motor battery positive
GND	Motor battery negative and Arduino GND
Remove the ENA and ENB jumpers when using D5 and D6 for speed control.
3. Ultrasonic sensor (HC-SR04)
HC-SR04	Arduino Uno
VCC	5V
GND	GND
TRIG	D11
ECHO	D12
4. Soil-moisture sensor
If you have a bare sensor with two metal prongs:
Connection	Where
Arduino 5V	One end of a 10 kΩ resistor
Other end of resistor	Arduino A0 and first probe prong
Second probe prong	GND
If yours has a circuit board with AO, DO, VCC and GND, stop here—the wiring is different.
5. Water pump
Use a suitable logic-level N-channel MOSFET, a 220 Ω resistor, a 10 kΩ resistor, and a flyback diode.
Connection	Where
Arduino D4	Through 220 Ω to MOSFET gate
MOSFET gate	Through 10 kΩ to GND
MOSFET source	Common GND
MOSFET drain	Pump negative
Pump positive	External pump-supply positive
Pump-supply negative	Common GND
Diode striped end (cathode)	Pump positive
Diode other end (anode)	Pump negative
Do not power the pump or drive motors directly from the Arduino.
6. Common ground
Connect these grounds together:
- Arduino GND
- L298N GND
- Motor battery negative
- Pump supply negative
- Sensor GND
